      "explanation": "Nitration is an electrophilic substitution reaction. So, the group which increase the electron density on benzene ring will increase the electrophilic substitution reaction.\n<br><br>Here <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> OCH<sub>3</sub> group shows + R effect, but <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> CH<sub>3</sub> group shows + I effect. As + R effect is more effective than + I effect so <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> OCH<sub>3</sub> will increase more electron density on benzene ring. \n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Cl has strong electron withdrawing effect (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> I). So it decrease electron density on the benzene ring. \n<br><br> In acidic medium, aniline form anilinium ion.\n<br><br><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l7u8h5xi/6bc467fc-20e8-401e-a0e6-81dc92e752ca/cb766e60-301b-11ed-ab58-4f43f7f8c851/file-1l7u8h5xj.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l7u8h5xi/6bc467fc-20e8-401e-a0e6-81dc92e752ca/cb766e60-301b-11ed-ab58-4f43f7f8c851/file-1l7u8h5xj.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2018 (Online) 15th April Morning Slot Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 235 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l7u8h5xi/6bc467fc-20e8-401e-a0e6-81dc92e752ca/cb766e60-301b-11ed-ab58-4f43f7f8c851/file-1l7u8h5xj.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l7u8h5xi/6bc467fc-20e8-401e-a0e6-81dc92e752ca/cb766e60-301b-11ed-ab58-4f43f7f8c851/file-1l7u8h5xj.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l7u8h5xi/6bc467fc-20e8-401e-a0e6-81dc92e752ca/cb766e60-301b-11ed-ab58-4f43f7f8c851/file-1l7u8h5xj.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l7u8h5xi/6bc467fc-20e8-401e-a0e6-81dc92e752ca/cb766e60-301b-11ed-ab58-4f43f7f8c851/file-1l7u8h5xj.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l7u8h5xi/6bc467fc-20e8-401e-a0e6-81dc92e752ca/cb766e60-301b-11ed-ab58-4f43f7f8c851/file-1l7u8h5xj.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l7u8h5xi/6bc467fc-20e8-401e-a0e6-81dc92e752ca/cb766e60-301b-11ed-ab58-4f43f7f8c851/file-1l7u8h5xj.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"><br>This anilinium ion is least reactive as in benzene ring electron density is least.\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>   The increasing order is (a) &lt; (b) &lt; (d) &lt; (c)"
